// The Supabase PUBLISHABLE key.
//
// ── read this before changing anything here ──────────────────────────────
// This value ships to the browser, and that is correct. A publishable key
// (formerly the "anon" key) identifies the project and grants nothing on its
// own — every table is protected by Row Level Security, which is what actually
// decides who may read and write. See supabase/schema.sql; those policies are
// the security boundary of this site, not this string.
//
// The SECRET key is a different thing entirely. It BYPASSES Row Level
// Security: anyone holding it can read and write every row in the database,
// including every applicant's name, telephone number and email address. It
// must never appear in this file, in this repository, or anywhere a browser
// can reach. If one is ever pasted here by mistake, rotate it in the dashboard
// immediately — a key committed to git has leaked, even after the commit is
// deleted.
//
// The two are easy to tell apart by their prefix:
//
//   sb_publishable_…   belongs here
//   sb_secret_…        never belongs here
//
// (Older projects use JWTs instead, where the payload says "role":"anon" or
// "role":"service_role". Same rule: only the first belongs here.)
export const SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = "sb_publishable_2Lh8X-fWvlJQFvpYSLB6Nw_1jKf3DSt";
